  "comment": "Class properties — bindings, defaults, aggregation (SCHEMA.md, NORMATIVE 2026-09-27). A property schema 'priority' is bound on classes Task (default 'medium') and Project (default 'high'). A node created with Task reads Task's default; assigning Project too (the OR-Set add carrier is a re-issued object.create on the same id) aggregates both bindings — the conflict resolves first-class-applied-wins, so Task's 'medium' (earlier assignment HLC) beats Project's 'high'. Unsetting Task's binding removes it from the aggregation, so the node's effective priority becomes Project's 'high'. Defaults are a DERIVED read model: no property_value rows are ever written for them.",
